"The Art of the Umayyad Period (661–750) - The Metropolitan Museum of Art (https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/the-art-of-the-umayyad-period-661-750)\nciteturn30view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/the-art-of-the-umayyad-period-661-750\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 162\nL0: [Button: Skip to main content]\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Tickets†engage.metmuseum.org】\nL3: \nL4: Select language\nL5: \nL6: English\nL7: \nL8: [Input]\nL9: \nL10: [Input]\nL11: \nL12: 【1†Donate†engage.metmuseum.org】【2†Membership†engage.metmuseum.org】【0†Tickets†engage.metmuseum.org】\nL13: \nL14:   * Visit\nL15:   * Exhibitions and Events\nL16:   * Art\nL17:   * Learn with Us\nL18:   * Research\nL19:   * 【3†Shop†store.metmuseum.org】\nL20:   * 【4†Timeline of Art History】\nL21: # The Art of the Umayyad Period (661–750)\nL22: \nL23: The Umayyad period is often considered the formative period in Islamic art.\nL24: \nL25: Linda Komaroff and Suzan Yalman\nL26: \nL27: October 1, 2001\nL28: \nL29: 【5†Image: Vessel with Pierced Designs, Bronze; pierced and chased†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL30: \nL31: 【6†Vessel with Pierced Designs】\nL32: \nL33: ca. 700\nL34: \nL35: 【7†Image: Slab, Ink on limestone†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL36: \nL37: 【8†Slab】\nL38: \nL39: first half 8th century\nL40: \nL41: 【9†Image: Woven Tapestry Fragment, Wool; tapestry weave†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL42: 【10†Woven Tapestry Fragment】\nL43: \nL44: mid-8th century\nL45: \nL46: 【11†Image: Ewer with a Cock-Shaped Spout, Bronze; cast and pierced†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL47: \nL48: 【12†Ewer with a Cock-Shaped Spout】\nL49: \nL50: 8th–early 9th century\nL51: After the death of 【13†Muhammad】 in 632, a series of four caliphs (Arabic: khalifa, “successor”), known as the Rightly Guided, succeeded. Under their command, the Arab armies carried the new faith from Arabia to the shores of the Mediterranean and to the eastern reaches of Iran. However, following the assassination of ‘Ali ibn Abi Talib—Muhammad’s cousin, son-in-law, and fourth caliph (r.\nL52: 656–61)—in 661, Mu‘awiya, the governor of Syria under the Rightly Guided Caliphs, seized power and established the Umayyad caliphate, the first Islamic dynasty (661–750). During Mu‘awiya’s reign (661–80), the seat of Islamic power was transferred from the Arabian Peninsula to Syria. Under Mu‘awiya’s successors, the important historic city of 【14†Damascus】 was transformed into the capital of an empire that extended 【15†from the Atlantic Ocean】 to the Indus River.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Art of the Abbasid Period (750–1258) - The Metropolitan Museum of Art (https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/the-art-of-the-abbasid-period-750-1258)\nciteturn30view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/the-art-of-the-abbasid-period-750-1258\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 168\nL0: [Button: Skip to main content]\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Tickets†engage.metmuseum.org】\nL3: \nL4: Select language\nL5: \nL6: English\nL7: \nL8: [Input]\nL9: \nL10: [Input]\nL11: \nL12: 【1†Donate†engage.metmuseum.org】【2†Membership†engage.metmuseum.org】【0†Tickets†engage.metmuseum.org】\nL13: \nL14:   * Visit\nL15:   * Exhibitions and Events\nL16:   * Art\nL17:   * Learn with Us\nL18:   * Research\nL19:   * 【3†Shop†store.metmuseum.org】\nL20:   * 【4†Timeline of Art History】\nL21: # The Art of the Abbasid Period (750–1258)\nL22: \nL23: During this period, a distinctive style emerged and new techniques were developed that spread throughout the Muslim realm and greatly influenced Islamic art and architecture.\nL24: \nL25: Linda Komaroff and Suzan Yalman\nL26: \nL27: October 1, 2001\nL28: \nL29: 【5†Image: Capital in the \"Beveled Style\", Alabaster, gypsum; carved†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL30: \nL31: 【6†Capital in the \"Beveled Style\"】\nL32: \nL33: late 8th century\nL34: 【7†Image: Pair of Doors Carved in the 'Beveled Style', Wood (teak); carved†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL35: \nL36: 【8†Pair of Doors Carved in the 'Beveled Style'】\nL37: \nL38: 9th century\nL39: \nL40: 【9†Image: Folio from a Qur'an Manuscript, Ink and gold on parchment†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL41: \nL42: 【10†Folio from a Qur'an Manuscript】\nL43: \nL44: late 9th–early 10th century\nL45: \nL46: 【11†Image: Bowl depicting a Man holding a Cup and a Flowering Branch, Earthenware; luster-painted on opaque white glaze†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL47: 【12†Bowl depicting a Man holding a Cup and a Flowering Branch】\nL48: \nL49: 10th century\nL50: \nL51: 【13†Image: <Tiraz> Textile Fragment, Cotton; plain weave, painted†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL52: \nL53: 【14†Textile Fragment】\nL54: \nL55: late 10th century\nL56: \nL57: 【15†Image: \"Preparing Medicine from Honey\", from a Dispersed Manuscript of an Arabic Translation of De Materia Medica of Dioscorides, 'Abdullah ibn al-Fadl , Baghdad, Ink, opaque watercolor, and gold on paper†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL58: 【16†\"Preparing Medicine from Honey\", from a Dispersed Manuscript of an Arabic Translation of De Materia Medica of Dioscorides】\nL59: \nL60: 'Abdullah ibn al-Fadl\nL61: \nL62: dated 621 AH/1224 CE\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Art of the Ottomans before 1600 - The Metropolitan Museum of Art (https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/the-art-of-the-ottomans-before-1600)\nciteturn30view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/the-art-of-the-ottomans-before-1600\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 248\nL0: [Button: Skip to main content]\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Tickets†engage.metmuseum.org】\nL3: \nL4: Select language\nL5: \nL6: English\nL7: \nL8: [Input]\nL9: \nL10: [Input]\nL11: \nL12: 【1†Donate†engage.metmuseum.org】【2†Membership†engage.metmuseum.org】【0†Tickets†engage.metmuseum.org】\nL13: \nL14:   * Visit\nL15:   * Exhibitions and Events\nL16:   * Art\nL17:   * Learn with Us\nL18:   * Research\nL19:   * 【3†Shop†store.metmuseum.org】\nL20:   * 【4†Timeline of Art History】\nL21: # The Art of the Ottomans before 1600\nL22: \nL23: With the conquest of the Mamluk empire in 1517, the Ottomans ruled over the most powerful state in the Islamic world.\nL24: \nL25: Suzan Yalman\nL26: \nL27: October 1, 2002\nL28: \nL29: 【5†Image: Fragmentary Silk Velvet with Repeating Tiger-stripe and 'Chintamani' Design, Silk, metal wrapped thread; cut and voided velvet (çatma), brocaded†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL30: \nL31: 【6†Fragmentary Silk Velvet with Repeating Tiger-stripe and 'Chintamani' Design】\nL32: \nL33: second half 15th century\nL34: 【7†Image: Mirror with Split-Leaf Palmette Design Inlaid with Gold, Iron, inlaid with gold; ivory†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL35: \nL36: 【8†Mirror with Split-Leaf Palmette Design Inlaid with Gold】\nL37: \nL38: early 16th century\nL39: \nL40: 【9†Image: Tile, Tempered earthenware; molded; polychrome glazed within black wax resist outlines (cuerda seca technique); gilded†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL41: \nL42: 【10†Tile】\nL43: \nL44: dated 824 AH/1421 CE\nL45: 【11†Image: Hungarian-Style Shield, Wood, leather, gesso, polychromy, Eastern European†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL46: \nL47: 【12†Hungarian-Style Shield】\nL48: \nL49: Eastern European\nL50: \nL51: ca. 1500–1550\nL52: \nL53: 【13†Image: Khusrau and Shirin, Hatifi Iranian, active Istanbul, Main support: ink, opaque watercolor, and gold on paper; binding: leather†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL54: \nL55: 【14†Khusrau and Shirin】\nL56: \nL57: Poet Hatifi\nL58: \nL59: Calligraphy, illumination, and painting by Suzi\nL60: \nL61: dated 904 AH/1498–99 CE\nL62: 【15†Image: Fragmentary Loom Width with Wavy-Vine Pattern, Silk, metal wrapped thread; lampas (kemha)†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL63: \nL64: 【16†Fragmentary Loom Width with Wavy-Vine Pattern】\nL65: \nL66: ca. 1565–80\nL67: \nL68: 【17†Image: 'Saz'-Style Drawing of a Dragon Amid Foliage, Shah Quli Turkish, Ink, opaque watercolor, and gold on paper†collectionapi.metmuseum.org】\nL69: \nL70: 【18†'Saz'-Style Drawing of a Dragon Amid Foliage】\nL71: \nL72: Shah Quli\nL73: \nL74: ca. 1540–50\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSahih al-Bukhari 6094 - Good Manners and Form (Al-Adab) - كتاب الأدب - Sunnah.com - Sayings and Teachings of Prophet Muhammad (صلى الله عليه و سلم) (https://sunnah.com/bukhari%3A6094)\nciteturn30view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6094\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6094; Total lines: 81\nL0: Contribute to our mission 【0†Donate Now】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Qur'an†quran.com】 | 【2†Sunnah】 | 【3†Prayer Times†salah.com】 | 【4†Audio†quranicaudio.com】\nL3: \nL4: 【5†Image: toggle Light Thme】 【6†Image: toggle Dark Thme】\nL5: \nL6: [Input: Search …] [Input]\nL7: ## Select Collections\nL8: \nL9: Sahih al-Bukhari\nL10: \nL11: Sahih Muslim\nL12: \nL13: Sunan an-Nasa'i\nL14: \nL15: Sunan Abi Dawud\nL16: \nL17: Jami` at-Tirmidhi\nL18: \nL19: Sunan Ibn Majah\nL20: \nL21: Show More Collections\nL22: \nL23: [Button: Apply]\nL24: \nL25: Quotes e.g. \"pledge allegiance\"\nL26: Searches for the whole phrase instead of individual words\nL27: \nL28: Wildcards e.g. test*\nL29: Matches any set of one or more characters. For example test* would result in test, tester, testers, etc.\nL30: \nL31: Fuzzy Search e.g. swore~\nL32: Finds terms that are similar in spelling. For example swore~ would result in swore, snore, score, etc.\nL33: Term Boosting e.g. pledge^4 hijrah\nL34: Boosts words with higher relevance. Here, the word pledge will have higher weight than hijrah\nL35: \nL36: Boolean Operators e.g. (\"pledge allegiance\" OR \"shelter) AND prayer\nL37: Create complex phrase and word queries by using Boolean logic.\nL38: \nL39: 【7†More ...】\nL40: \nL41: 【2†Home】 » 【8†Sahih al-Bukhari】 » 【9†Good Manners and Form (Al-Adab) - كتاب الأدب】 » Hadith 6094\nL42: \nL43: Language:\nL44: \nL45: [Input] English\nL46: \nL47: [Input] Urdu  اردو\nL48: \nL49: [Input] Bangla  বাংলা\nL50: \nL51: كتاب الأدب\nL52: \nL53: 78\nL54: \nL55: Good Manners and Form (Al-Adab)\nL56: \nL57: (69)\nL58: Chapter: \"O you who believe! Be afraid of Allah, and be with those who are true\"\nL59: \nL60: (69)\nL61: \nL62: بَابُ قَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَكُونُوا مَعَ الصَّادِقِينَ} وَمَا يُنْهَى عَنِ الْكَذِبِ\nL63: \nL64: Sahih al-Bukhari 6094\nL65: \nL66: Narrated `Abdullah:\nL67: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \"Truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. And a man keeps on telling the truth until he becomes a truthful person. Falsehood leads to Al-Fajur (i.e. wickedness, evil-doing), and Al-Fajur (wickedness) leads to the (Hell) Fire, and a man may keep on telling lies till he is written before Allah, a liar.\"\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSahih al-Bukhari 6018 - Good Manners and Form (Al-Adab) - كتاب الأدب - Sunnah.com - Sayings and Teachings of Prophet Muhammad (صلى الله عليه و سلم) (https://sunnah.com/bukhari%3A6018)\nciteturn30view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6018\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6018; Total lines: 81\nL0: Contribute to our mission 【0†Donate Now】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Qur'an†quran.com】 | 【2†Sunnah】 | 【3†Prayer Times†salah.com】 | 【4†Audio†quranicaudio.com】\nL3: \nL4: 【5†Image: toggle Light Thme】 【6†Image: toggle Dark Thme】\nL5: \nL6: [Input: Search …] [Input]\nL7: ## Select Collections\nL8: \nL9: Sahih al-Bukhari\nL10: \nL11: Sahih Muslim\nL12: \nL13: Sunan an-Nasa'i\nL14: \nL15: Sunan Abi Dawud\nL16: \nL17: Jami` at-Tirmidhi\nL18: \nL19: Sunan Ibn Majah\nL20: \nL21: Show More Collections\nL22: \nL23: [Button: Apply]\nL24: \nL25: Quotes e.g. \"pledge allegiance\"\nL26: Searches for the whole phrase instead of individual words\nL27: \nL28: Wildcards e.g. test*\nL29: Matches any set of one or more characters. For example test* would result in test, tester, testers, etc.\nL30: \nL31: Fuzzy Search e.g. swore~\nL32: Finds terms that are similar in spelling. For example swore~ would result in swore, snore, score, etc.\nL33: Term Boosting e.g. pledge^4 hijrah\nL34: Boosts words with higher relevance. Here, the word pledge will have higher weight than hijrah\nL35: \nL36: Boolean Operators e.g. (\"pledge allegiance\" OR \"shelter) AND prayer\nL37: Create complex phrase and word queries by using Boolean logic.\nL38: \nL39: 【7†More ...】\nL40: \nL41: 【2†Home】 » 【8†Sahih al-Bukhari】 » 【9†Good Manners and Form (Al-Adab) - كتاب الأدب】 » Hadith 6018\nL42: \nL43: Language:\nL44: \nL45: [Input] English\nL46: \nL47: [Input] Urdu  اردو\nL48: \nL49: [Input] Bangla  বাংলা\nL50: \nL51: كتاب الأدب\nL52: \nL53: 78\nL54: \nL55: Good Manners and Form (Al-Adab)\nL56: \nL57: (31)\nL58: Chapter: Whosoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not harm his neighbor\nL59: \nL60: (31)\nL61: \nL62: باب مَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الآخِرِ فَلاَ يُؤْذِ جَارَهُ\nL63: \nL64: Sahih al-Bukhari 6018\nL65: \nL66: Narrated Abu Huraira:\nL67: Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, \"Anybody who believes in Allah and the Last Day should not harm his neighbor, and anybody who believes in Allah and the Last Day should entertain his guest generously and anybody who believes in Allah and the Last Day should talk what is good or keep quiet. (i.e. abstain from all kinds of evil and dirty talk).\nL68: حَدَّثَنَا 【10†قُتَيْبَةُ بْنُ سَعِيدٍ】، حَدَّثَنَا 【11†أَبُو الأَحْوَصِ】، عَنْ 【12†أَبِي حَصِينٍ】، عَنْ 【13†أَبِي صَالِحٍ】، عَنْ 【14†أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ】، قَالَ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏\"‏ مَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الآخِرِ فَلاَ يُؤْذِ جَارَهُ، وَمَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الآخِرِ فَلْيُكْرِمْ ضَيْفَهُ، وَمَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الآخِرِ فَلْيَقُلْ خَيْرًا أَوْ لِيَصْمُتْ ‏\"‏‏.‏\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSahih al-Bukhari 6114 - Good Manners and Form (Al-Adab) - كتاب الأدب - Sunnah.com - Sayings and Teachings of Prophet Muhammad (صلى الله عليه و سلم) (https://sunnah.com/bukhari%3A6114)\nciteturn30view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6114\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6114; Total lines: 82\nL0: Contribute to our mission 【0†Donate Now】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Qur'an†quran.com】 | 【2†Sunnah】 | 【3†Prayer Times†salah.com】 | 【4†Audio†quranicaudio.com】\nL3: \nL4: 【5†Image: toggle Light Thme】 【6†Image: toggle Dark Thme】\nL5: \nL6: [Input: Search …] [Input]\nL7: ## Select Collections\nL8: \nL9: Sahih al-Bukhari\nL10: \nL11: Sahih Muslim\nL12: \nL13: Sunan an-Nasa'i\nL14: \nL15: Sunan Abi Dawud\nL16: \nL17: Jami` at-Tirmidhi\nL18: \nL19: Sunan Ibn Majah\nL20: \nL21: Show More Collections\nL22: \nL23: [Button: Apply]\nL24: \nL25: Quotes e.g. \"pledge allegiance\"\nL26: Searches for the whole phrase instead of individual words\nL27: \nL28: Wildcards e.g. test*\nL29: Matches any set of one or more characters. For example test* would result in test, tester, testers, etc.\nL30: \nL31: Fuzzy Search e.g. swore~\nL32: Finds terms that are similar in spelling. For example swore~ would result in swore, snore, score, etc.\nL33: Term Boosting e.g. pledge^4 hijrah\nL34: Boosts words with higher relevance. Here, the word pledge will have higher weight than hijrah\nL35: \nL36: Boolean Operators e.g. (\"pledge allegiance\" OR \"shelter) AND prayer\nL37: Create complex phrase and word queries by using Boolean logic.\nL38: \nL39: 【7†More ...】\nL40: \nL41: 【2†Home】 » 【8†Sahih al-Bukhari】 » 【9†Good Manners and Form (Al-Adab) - كتاب الأدب】 » Hadith 6114\nL42: \nL43: Language:\nL44: \nL45: [Input] English\nL46: \nL47: [Input] Urdu  اردو\nL48: \nL49: [Input] Bangla  বাংলা\nL50: \nL51: كتاب الأدب\nL52: \nL53: 78\nL54: \nL55: Good Manners and Form (Al-Adab)\nL56: \nL57: (76)\nL58: Chapter: To be cautious from being angry\nL59: \nL60: (76)\nL61: \nL62: باب الْحَذَرِ مِنَ الْغَضَبِ\nL63: \nL64: Sahih al-Bukhari 6114\nL65: \nL66: Narrated Abu Huraira:\nL67: \nL68: Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, \"The strong is not the one who overcomes the people by his strength, but the strong is the one who controls himself while in anger.\"\nL69: حَدَّثَنَا 【10†عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ يُوسُفَ】، أَخْبَرَنَا 【11†مَالِكٌ】، عَنِ 【12†ابْنِ شِهَابٍ】، عَنْ 【13†سَعِيدِ بْنِ الْمُسَيَّبِ】، عَنْ 【14†أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ】 ـ رضى الله عنه ـ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم قَالَ ‏\"‏ لَيْسَ الشَّدِيدُ بِالصُّرَعَةِ، إِنَّمَا الشَّدِيدُ الَّذِي يَمْلِكُ نَفْسَهُ عِنْدَ الْغَضَبِ ‏\"‏‏.‏\nL70: Reference  |  : 【15†Sahih al-Bukhari 6114】\nL71: In-book reference  |  : Book 78, Hadith 141\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSahih al-Bukhari 5027 - Virtues of the Qur'an - كتاب فضائل القرآن - Sunnah.com - Sayings and Teachings of Prophet Muhammad (صلى الله عليه و سلم) (https://sunnah.com/bukhari%3A5027)\nciteturn30view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:5027\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://sunnah.com/bukhari:5027; Total lines: 82\nL0: Contribute to our mission 【0†Donate Now】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Qur'an†quran.com】 | 【2†Sunnah】 | 【3†Prayer Times†salah.com】 | 【4†Audio†quranicaudio.com】\nL3: \nL4: 【5†Image: toggle Light Thme】 【6†Image: toggle Dark Thme】\nL5: \nL6: [Input: Search …] [Input]\nL7: ## Select Collections\nL8: \nL9: Sahih al-Bukhari\nL10: \nL11: Sahih Muslim\nL12: \nL13: Sunan an-Nasa'i\nL14: \nL15: Sunan Abi Dawud\nL16: \nL17: Jami` at-Tirmidhi\nL18: \nL19: Sunan Ibn Majah\nL20: \nL21: Show More Collections\nL22: \nL23: [Button: Apply]\nL24: \nL25: